[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m                                            Large Language Models (LLMs) have recently demonstrated remarkable capabilities in natural language processing tasks and[m
[32m+[m[32m                                         beyond. This success of LLMs has led to a large influx of research contributions in this direction. These works encompass diverse[m
[32m+[m[32m                                         topics such as architectural innovations, better training strategies, context length improvements, fine-tuning, multi-modal LLMs,[m
[32m+[m[32m                                         robotics, datasets, benchmarking, efficiency, and more. With the rapid development of techniques and regular breakthroughs in[m
[32m+[m[32m                                         LLM research, it has become considerably challenging to perceive the bigger picture of the advances in this direction. Considering[m
[32m+[m[32m                                         the rapidly emerging plethora of literature on LLMs, it is imperative that the research community is able to benefit from a concise[m
[32m+[m[32m                                         yet comprehensive overview of the recent developments in this field. This article provides an overview of the literature on a broad[m
[32m+[m[32m                                         range of LLM-related concepts. Our self-contained comprehensive overview of LLMs discusses relevant background concepts[m
[32m+[m[32m                                         along with covering the advanced topics at the frontier of research in LLMs. This review article is intended to provide not only a[m
[32m+[m[32m                                         systematic survey but also a quick, comprehensive reference for the researchers and practitioners to draw insights from extensive,[m
[32m+[m[32m                                         informative summaries of the existing works to advance the LLM research.[m
